\documentclass{article}
\title{Aspect-Based Sentiment Analysis with Syntactic Cues}
\author{Anon}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Introduction}
Aspect-based sentiment analysis predicts the sentiment polarity toward a specific aspect in a sentence. We combine a dependency-tree encoder with a syntax-aware attention layer.
\section{Model}
The model encodes the sentence with a graph network over the dependency tree, then attends to nodes near the aspect term. Figure~\ref{fig:arch} shows the overall architecture. Figure~\ref{fig:attn} visualizes attention weights on a review sentence. Table~\ref{tab:main} reports accuracy and macro-F1 on three datasets.
